meta {
  name: Why a read would be served by one source and not another (dry run)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/sources/trace?capability=quotes&symbols=NSE:RELIANCE,NSE:NIFTY
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  capability: quotes
  symbols: NSE:RELIANCE,NSE:NIFTY
  ~purpose: display
  ~maxAgeMs: 0
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  Why a read would be served by one source and not another (dry run)

  - An API key with the `read` scope (any key).

  Runs the router's decision for a read and explains it: every candidate (your pooled broker accounts and the
  enabled sources), with the verdict (`chosen`, `fallback` or `skipped`), the reason, the score and the spare
  budget. Nothing is fetched and no upstream call is made, so it costs no quota. `class` is the data class the
  answer would carry.

  Reference: docs/api/sources/traceSources.md in the repository.
}
